From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui/cocoa: a display leaving the VM's Space stays left

What: a click in an extra display's window hands the keyboard back to the
main window (only while the main window's Space shows). The extra
window no longer does that when it merely becomes key.

Why: with two displays, the escape combo moved the pointer's display to
the macOS Space beside the VM's, then it flicked straight back (user
report, 3.0.0 candidate, 2026-10-06). When the main window's Space leaves
its display, macOS makes the app's other window (on the other display)
key; that window gave the key back to the main window, which is on a Space
not shown, and macOS switched the display back to it to show it. Checking
the Space when the window became key depended on the order in which macOS
changes the key window and the Space (independent review, 2026-10-06); at
the click there is no such order.

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's omacvm-cocoa-displays.patch).
Test: Tests/display/test-fullscreen-space.sh (build time) and the live
two-display check on the Mac mini (tracks: fullscreen-space). Applies
after omacvm-cocoa-fullscreen-own-space.patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -6427,19 +6427,46 @@ - (void)mouseMoved:(NSEvent *)e { [self send:e button:-1 down:false]; }
 - (void)mouseDragged:(NSEvent *)e { [self send:e button:-1 down:false]; }
 - (void)rightMouseDragged:(NSEvent *)e { [self send:e button:-1 down:false]; }
 - (void)otherMouseDragged:(NSEvent *)e { [self send:e button:-1 down:false]; }
-- (void)mouseDown:(NSEvent *)e { [self send:e button:INPUT_BUTTON_LEFT down:true]; }
+/*
+ * A click here made this window key. The keyboard and the main window's
+ * pointer tracking belong to the main window: hand it back, at the click
+ * (not when this window becomes key: macOS also makes it key when the escape
+ * combo or a swipe moves the main window's display to another Space, and
+ * making the main window key then switched that display straight back).
+ * Only while the main window's Space shows. The click still goes to the VM.
+ */
+- (void)handKeyBack
+{
+    NSWindow *main = [cocoaView window];
+    if ([main isVisible] && [main isOnActiveSpace] && [NSApp isActive] && ![main isKeyWindow]) {
+        [main makeKeyWindow];
+    }
+}
+- (void)mouseDown:(NSEvent *)e
+{
+    [self handKeyBack];
+    [self send:e button:INPUT_BUTTON_LEFT down:true];
+}
 - (void)mouseUp:(NSEvent *)e
 {
     [self send:e button:INPUT_BUTTON_LEFT down:false];
     [cocoaView omacvmUngrabAfterDrag];
 }
-- (void)rightMouseDown:(NSEvent *)e { [self send:e button:INPUT_BUTTON_RIGHT down:true]; }
+- (void)rightMouseDown:(NSEvent *)e
+{
+    [self handKeyBack];
+    [self send:e button:INPUT_BUTTON_RIGHT down:true];
+}
 - (void)rightMouseUp:(NSEvent *)e
 {
     [self send:e button:INPUT_BUTTON_RIGHT down:false];
     [cocoaView omacvmUngrabAfterDrag];
 }
-- (void)otherMouseDown:(NSEvent *)e { [self send:e button:INPUT_BUTTON_MIDDLE down:true]; }
+- (void)otherMouseDown:(NSEvent *)e
+{
+    [self handKeyBack];
+    [self send:e button:INPUT_BUTTON_MIDDLE down:true];
+}
 - (void)otherMouseUp:(NSEvent *)e
 {
     [self send:e button:INPUT_BUTTON_MIDDLE down:false];
@@ -6546,21 +6573,6 @@ - (NSApplicationPresentationOptions)window:(NSWindow *)window
                                 NSApplicationPresentationAutoHideMenuBar)) |
            NSApplicationPresentationHideDock | NSApplicationPresentationHideMenuBar;
 }
-
-/*
- * A click on another display's window makes it key. The keyboard and the
- * main window's pointer tracking belong to the main window: hand it back.
- * The click itself still reaches this window's view.
- */
-- (void)windowDidBecomeKey:(NSNotification *)note
-{
-    dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), ^{
-        NSWindow *main = [cocoaView window];
-        if ([main isVisible] && [NSApp isActive] && ![main isKeyWindow]) {
-            [main makeKeyWindow];
-        }
-    });
-}
 @end
 
 static OmacVMHeadDelegate *omacvm_head_delegate;
